### **9. Neon-Specific Optimizations**

For better performance with Neon, add this to your `.env`:

```env
# Direct connection URL for migrations (bypasses connection pooler)
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://username:password@ep-xyz.region.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require"

# Connection pooler for application queries
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://username:password@ep-xyz.region.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require&pgbouncer=true"
```

### **10. Add Neon-Specific Indexes**

Create a migration for performance optimizations:

```bash
npx prisma migrate dev --name add_performance_indexes
```

In the migration file, add:

```sql
-- Performance indexes for ecommerce
CREATE INDEX idx_products_vendor ON "Product"("vendorId");
CREATE INDEX idx_products_category ON "Product"("categoryId");
CREATE INDEX idx_products_price ON "Product"("basePrice");
CREATE INDEX idx_products_active ON "Product"("isActive") WHERE "isActive" = true;
CREATE INDEX idx_products_featured ON "Product"("isFeatured") WHERE "isFeatured" = true;

-- Full-text search index
CREATE INDEX idx_products_search ON "Product" USING GIN(
  to_tsvector('english', "title" || ' ' || "description")
);

-- Order indexes
CREATE INDEX idx_orders_user ON "Order"("userId");
CREATE INDEX idx_orders_status ON "Order"("status");
CREATE INDEX idx_orders_created ON "Order"("createdAt" DESC);

-- Inventory indexes
CREATE INDEX idx_inventory_product ON "ProductInventory"("productId");
CREATE INDEX idx_inventory_low_stock ON "ProductInventory"("quantity") WHERE "quantity" <= "lowStockThreshold";
```

## **Development Workflow**

### **Database Branching (Neon Feature)**

```bash
# Create a development branch
npx neonctl branches create clicon-dev --parent-id your-project-id

# Switch to development branch
# Update DATABASE_URL to point to dev branch
```

### **Local Development**

```bash
# Start development server
npm run dev

# Monitor database queries
npx prisma studio

# Reset database (careful!)
npx prisma migrate reset
```

## **Production Deployment**

### **Vercel Integration**

1. Install Vercel Neon integration
2. Add environment variables in Vercel:
   ```
   DATABASE_URL=your-neon-production-url
   DIRECT_URL=your-neon-direct-url
   BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=your-production-secret
   ```

### **Connection Pooling**

For production, use Neon's connection pooler:

```env
# Production DATABASE_URL with connection pooling
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://username:password@ep-xyz.region.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require&pgbouncer=true&max_connections=10"
```

